// =======================================================================================
//          ============================= /FORCEPOWERS =============================
// =======================================================================================

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_BH
NOTES               "Bounty Hunter"
LANG_ENGLISH        "^4BOUNTY HUNTER^7\nA marksman and skirmisher class specializing in long-range combat. Armed with two powerful sniper rifle options capable of eliminating targets in a single shot, combined with exceptional movement speed, the Bounty Hunter is a threat to every Rebel class.\n\n^2> Weapons\n- \rPistol\r\n^7With low firerate, high damage and full accuracy the pistol is a high skill ceiling option capable of quickly dispatching enemies.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks an alternate charged fire mode.\n-- Level 3: Grants a high-powered primary fire and charge mode with increased ammo consumption. Toggle weapon mode to revert to the standard pistol.\n\n- \rE-11 Blaster\r\n^7The E-11 is a very versatile blaster rifle featuring two firing modes, a slow firing primary fire, which deals higher damage and is of higher velocity, and secondary fire for close range engagements.\n-- Level 1: A standard blaster rifle with slow primary fire and high velocity.\n-- Level 2: Adds a faster firing alt. fire.\n-- Level 3: Makes alt.fire accurate when walking and standing still, and increases the clip capacity.\n\n- \rDLT-20a\r\n^7A slow-firing rifle with modest damage on its own, the DLT-20a becomes a powerhouse through its burst fire mode\n-- Level 1: A medium-powered high-velocity rifle.\n-- Level 2: Adds a burst mode (toggle with Weapon Mode key).\n-- Level 3: Adds a scope on the alt. fire button.\n\n- \rProjectile Rifle\r\nA dedicated sniper weapon that cannot be upgraded. Features two zoom levels switched with weapon mode. Must always be fired while scoped, jumping while scoped is not possible, and the rifle is only accurate when standing completely still.\n\n- \rDisruptor\r\nA slow-firing hitscan weapon with perfect accuracy at all times. When scoped, it transforms into a charged sniper capable of tearing through targets.\n-- Level 1: Unscoped hit-scan shot and a scope.\n-- Level 2: Allows a charged shot whilst scoped. Can shoot through multiple targets.\n\n^3> Abilities & Utility^7 \n- Advanced Melee\nBounty hunter can use melee moves with their weapon drawn. Use Class Special 1 combined with a movement key to perform a kick, CS1 + Crouch to perform a sweep kick, or Forward + Use + CS1 to air-kick. Use these moves to catch a Jedi off-guard and knock them down when they get close.\n\n- \rThermal Detonator\r\nA grenade which disintegrates anything within its blast radius.\n\n- \rPoison Dart\r ^3[Class Special 1 in Melee]^7\nPoison darts do a small amount of damage every second over a period of time. They also slow down Force pool regeneration. 1 dart available per level (max. 3).\n\n- \rTracking Dart\r ^3[Class Special 2 in Melee]^7\nTracker darts allow you to track one or more targets through walls etc. Tracked targets will periodically flash with the color depending on their health level (green – healthy, red – heavily wounded). Comes in packs of 2 (max. 6 darts)."

ENDMARKER